    "updated_at": "2020-03-18T20:59:44Z",
    "body": "Correct. It behaves similarly to the memory usage module, which is disabled by default. Memory usage is disabled by default since most people don't see immediate value in knowing the RAM usage. For those who do, the default behavior is only to show it when it is over 75% used. That behavior can be configured with the `memory_usage.threshold` configuration value.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
